        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This should now be resolved on latest `main`. Thanks again for noticing it!\n\nIt took a lot more time to fix that usually, because I wasn't really sure about the best approach here. Returning and using a copy of any object is used pretty much in all of 'mini.nvim'. So uniformly switching to some custom (re)implementation of `vim.deepcopy()` seems to be too much.\n\nIn the end, I only settled on the small one-liner re-implementation (which is fortunate) and using it only in places where *any* custom data can be present. Currently only on 'mini.pick' (because of this issue), but maybe it makes sense to do an overhaul of all modules that can carry any type of custom data to use custom reimplementation instead.",
